        <mxCell id="eYToQM8D4CzLMdLLenoR-50" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFA500;verticalAlign=middle;movable=1;resizable=1;rotatable=1;deletable=1;editable=1;locked=0;connectable=1;fontColor=default;fontSize=14;" value="Internal CAN bus" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="28" width="120" x="-225" y="275.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eYToQM8D4CzLMdLLenoR-92" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;Functional requirements:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;FR-01: Unauthorized diagnostic commands related to reprogramming must be filtered&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;QA&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Security: MM message route is just in IP, not EP.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Security&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Maintainability&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;================================================================================================&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;RDG will handling SID from server and CDC.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In the CDC case, If RDG is in the ip?, then CDC SID message route is just in the IP. not EP. that is good for security.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;You need to understand why EP and IP separation.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Basically, TMC think that ECU of external point (communicate with server) has the security risk.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;But they belive if the seaprated partition that is not communicate with server directlry, this will be safer.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;So, CDC is currently securable ECU, they just want to communicate with IP, not EP.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In the TMC requrement, they just assume that the situation only EP partion has the compromized area.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;02. EP/Internal Partition (Container) - &amp;lt;VS스마트제품개발담당&amp;gt; TOYOTA DCM - Collaboration Center&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;p&gt;Previsous version was there are two RDG&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;RDG in EP - to handle SIDs from Server and send SIDs to InternalRDG&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;InternalRDG in IP - to handle SIDs from CDC&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Security team of TMC was agreed this architecture as the security view point.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But RDG team of TMC dose not want to saparate RDG.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;So RDG has moved into ip&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;RDG team prefer to one app. they think that separte RDG is not good to manage and not necessary.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="704" width="857" x="-1176" y="1123" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eYToQM8D4CzLMdLLenoR-94" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#0000CC;container=0;movable=1;resizable=1;rotatable=1;deletable=1;editable=1;locked=0;connectable=1;strokeWidth=2;" value="&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;LXC container&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;IP Container&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="492" width="352" x="-727.75" y="2224" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
